    "n1": {"x": 2820, "y": 0, "w": 380, "fill": "orange", "text": "Design notes\n\n• Same look as Crossix: cream ground, glass panels, rounded numerals, the floating menu circle top right.\n• Digital cards only. Setup picks This phone or Online, 2 to 6 players, and 1 to 4 decks shuffled together.\n• Draw for first turn: everyone draws one card, highest rank starts. Equal ranks of different suits tie and only those players draw again. No dice anywhere.\n• Each player picks a card style (12 colour and pattern backs). The colour of the back is that player's colour everywhere; two players can't hold the same style. Names on a player colour use dark or white ink, whichever passes 4.5:1.\n• Online turns pass by themselves as soon as a play or pickup resolves. Next Turn appears only on one phone, where the device changes hands.\n• Online, every other player is a compact panel across the top; the one to move is ringed in their colour.\n• The handoff screen shows no cards at all, and it is also what appears after a refresh."}
